  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Long Loop – passing to a player at pace",
  "description": "A line in each corner and a goalkeeper in both goals. A runs at high tempo up into the other half, makes a big loop and turns back towards their own goal. At the same time B takes a few steps out of the corner and gets a pass from D. B carries the ball a few steps and passes to A, who receives at pace and goes for goal. After the pass B curves in towards the middle and becomes the next runner.\n\nRotation: A to C, C to A, B to D and D to B. Run it from the other corners at the same time.\n\nEasier variant: skip the middle station – B plays the long pass straight from the corner to A, who shoots and goes to the back of the same line. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The receiver shows with the stick where the pass should go."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The pass should stay on the floor, without bouncing, and be played into A's path."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Receive without losing speed and drive in towards goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "High tempo in the loop – the shots should hit the target."
    }
  ],
